{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:02ce407401a220e5","name":"Police Officer","source":{"id":"source:reference-02ce407401a220e5","title":"Police Officer","revision":18995,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:06:23Z","sha256":"82902cf16e7ebd17103d106bcd7344eeb344ebdccf5ed26eaba002b87ecead0b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18995","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Police%20Officer&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-02ce407401a220e5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Police Officers are charged with keeping the peace and enforcing laws. Depending on each world and its laws, a Police Officer can be anything from little more than a monitor who has little authority to a brutal instrument of the state. The vast majority of Police Officers fall in the middle ground. They have the authority to detain suspicious individuals, make arrests (with sufficient evidence), and use deadly force in self-defense or to protect bystanders from harm.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Most Police Officers are overworked and underpaid, but continue to do an otherwise thankless job for the sake of keeping the streets safe. Customs and laws of various worlds make bribery a possibility when dealing with Police Officers- minor violations might be overlooked for the right amount of credits.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The statistics provided here can be used for security guards, private defense contractors, and other individuals dedicated to community protection.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Police Officer Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Police Officers typically wear ",{"tag":"a","children":["Light Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Light_Armor","referenceId":"reference:1b329ddc8a34adfe"}," and carry sidearms, which is enough protection and firepower to deal with regular criminals and to deter suspects from doing anything drastic. Many Police Officers are required to keep their blasters on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," Setting as a means of preventing unnecessary fatalities. They also carry ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun Batons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun_Batons"}," for close combat.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Most Police Officers assigned to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," also carry more powerful (or specialized) weapons to deal with bigger threats. A Police \"Cruiser\" typically carries a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:fb78a988cbf9557f"},", an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:a21c35934de9acbe"},", three ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun Grenades"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun_Grenades"},", and an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Grenade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Grenade","referenceId":"reference:df3e0192b05e2e63"},". On more authoritarian or violent worlds, Police Officers have their weapons deal lethal damage and commonly use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rifles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rifles","referenceId":"reference:a6ebe3ecc8b0b281"}," and heavier ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Police Officers are usually assigned to work in pairs and are under standing orders to call for backup if things become dangerous. On average, additional Police Officers arrive within 1d10 minutes after a call is made. Wealthier worlds also team Police Officers with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," to provide additional firepower or reduce the chance of an officer getting injured. These ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," are linked into the local precinct's systems, sending a constant stream of information back for use as evidence.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Police Officer Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +7\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 15 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 14), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 10, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 14, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 6 Squares\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unarmed"],